 ```
 
+#### Max Loss Streak
+
+`MaxLossStreak` counts how many closed trades in a row resulted in a loss (a trade counts as a loss when `close_profit` is below `required_profit`, which defaults to `0.0`), looking only at the most recent trades within `lookback_period` (in minutes, or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`). A single trade that isn't a loss resets the streak.
+
+Once `trade_limit` losses have happened back-to-back, trading is stopped for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+By default, this both locks the affected pair once it has `trade_limit` consecutive losses (`stop_per_pair`), and locks all pairs bot-wide once the same number of losses has happened in a row across all pairs combined (`global_stop`), regardless of which pair each losing trade was on. Setting `only_per_pair` to `true` disables the bot-wide lock, leaving only the per-pair behavior.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of consecutive long losses.
+
+Since the per-pair and bot-wide checks share the same `trade_limit` / `stop_duration` for a given protection entry, define the protection twice - once with `only_per_pair: true` - if you want different thresholds or cooldowns for the per-pair and bot-wide cases.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair (and the whole bot) for 4 candles after 3 consecutive losing trades within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxLossStreak",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 #### Cooldown Period
 
 `CooldownPeriod` locks a pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) after exiting, avoiding a re-entry for this pair for `stop_duration` minutes.
